# Line endings are LF everywhere: oxfmt writes LF, and this keeps Windows
# checkouts from re-introducing CRLF through core.autocrlf.
* text=auto eol=lf
# ... except the launcher (#85). cmd.exe reads a `.bat` line by line and its
# label/goto and block parsing expect CRLF; a batch file that fits the rest of
# the repository's LF rule is the kind of thing that works on one machine and
# silently skips a line on another. `-text` stores and checks out the bytes the
# packaging ticket (#86) copies into the archive verbatim.
*.bat -text
